//@version=6
// ==============================================================================================
//                    A D A P T I V E   S U P P O R T   R E S I S T A N C E
// ==============================================================================================
//
//  Indicator Name : Adaptive Support Resistance
//  Author         : Forex_Market_Insights
//  Version        : v6.1 - July 2026
//  Pine Version   : Pine Script v6
//  Script Type    : Overlay indicator (plots on the price chart)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A U T H O R   V E R I F I C A T I O N   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I am Forex_Market_Insights, the publisher and sole original author of this exact
//  implementation of "Adaptive Support Resistance." I designed the architecture of this tool,
//  wrote every line of the Pine Script v6 code contained in this file, tested it across multiple
//  asset classes and timeframes, and I take full and sole ownership and responsibility for it.
//
//  Specifically, I independently designed and coded: the volatility-adaptive swing confirmation
//  window that widens and narrows itself with market conditions; the manual pivot qualification
//  routine that operates on that dynamic window; the four-component Level Power model built from
//  displacement impulse, participation multiple, rejection quality and recency decay; the
//  ATR-relative normalisation that makes that power score comparable across every instrument and
//  price magnitude; the clustering engine that merges nearby swings and converts repeat touches
//  into confirmation weight; the zone model that expresses each level as a volatility-scaled band
//  rather than a single price; the role-reversal engine that flips a broken level to the opposite
//  side and keeps trading it; the higher-timeframe confluence layer and its power bonus; the
//  psychological round-number engine with automatic step selection; the live hold-rate statistics
//  that report how often each power tier has actually held on this chart; the ATR-based proximity
//  classification; the seven-state pressure meter with optional smoothing; the Universal Activity
//  Engine that keeps the participation component alive on feeds with no volume; the complete
//  label, zone and summary table presentation; and the alert framework.
//
//  This declaration is made for this specific version of the script (v6.1, July 2026). Any future
//  modified version I publish will carry its own updated declaration in this same header.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  O R I G I N A L   I N D I C A T O R   S C R I P T   I M P L E M E N T A T I O N
//  V E R I F I C A T I O N   A N D   D E C L A R A T I O N
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I verify and declare that this script is an original implementation authored from scratch by
//  Forex_Market_Insights. No portion of this code was copied, ported, decompiled, translated,
//  reverse-engineered or adapted from any other author's closed-source, invite-only, protected or
//  open-source script. No third-party library and no republished open-source script forms any
//  part of this work, and no other author's scoring model or visual system was reproduced.
//
//  I acknowledge openly that the underlying trading concepts used here are public and widely
//  taught: swing highs and swing lows, horizontal support and resistance, support and resistance
//  expressed as zones rather than exact prices, the role reversal of a broken level, the extra
//  weight given to levels tested repeatedly, higher-timeframe confluence, the psychological pull
//  of round numbers, and the reading of a candle's closing position within its own range as a
//  proxy for who controlled that bar. These concepts belong to no single author.
//
//  My original contribution, and what this declaration covers, is the specific code
//  implementation: my own adaptive window formula, my own four-component power model and its
//  weighting, my own ATR-relative normalisation approach, my own clustering and touch
//  confirmation logic, my own zone construction, my own role-reversal state machine, my own
//  confluence bonus model, my own automatic round-number step selection, my own hold-rate
//  statistics engine, my own proximity classification, my own pressure state machine, and my own
//  presentation layer. Conceptual overlap with other support and resistance tools is therefore
//  unavoidable and expected, but there is no source-code overlap of any kind.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H Y   T H I S   T O O L   S C O R E S   L E V E L S   D I F F E R E N T L Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A common and serious flaw in level-scoring tools is to derive "strength" from a figure that
//  includes the raw price level itself, for example dividing price by ATR. On a low-priced pair
//  that produces a usable spread of scores, but on a high-priced instrument such as gold or an
//  index the figure immediately saturates its own ceiling and every single level reports the
//  maximum score. The output looks confident and is in fact meaningless, because it no longer
//  distinguishes anything.
//
//  This implementation contains no raw price term anywhere in its scoring. Power is built only
//  from ratios and from ATR-relative distances:
//
//    Displacement impulse  = size of the move into and away from the swing, divided by ATR
//    Participation         = activity on the swing bar, divided by its own recent average
//    Rejection quality     = wick beyond the body, divided by that bar's own range
//    Recency               = a decay factor based on how many bars ago the level formed
//    Touch confirmation    = a bonus per additional respected test of the same area
//    Confluence            = a bonus when a higher-timeframe level sits at the same price
//
//  Every one of those is dimensionless. A level scored 8 on gold means the same thing as a level
//  scored 8 on EURUSD or on a 30-second crypto chart, and weak levels genuinely report as weak.
// ==============================================================================================
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  W H A T   T H I S   I N D I C A T O R   D O E S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  1) ADAPTIVE SWING DETECTION
//     The number of bars required on each side of a candidate turning point is not fixed. The
//     engine measures current volatility against its own recent baseline and sets the
//     confirmation window between the configured minimum and maximum. In fast, expanding markets
//     fewer bars are required, because turns resolve quickly. In quiet, compressed markets more
//     bars are required, because drift produces false turns.
//
//  2) LEVEL POWER SCORE, 0 to 10
//     Each qualified swing is scored from dimensionless components only, described above. The
//     three primary components are weighted, combined and scaled to a 0 to 10 range, then
//     modified by recency decay, by confirmation from repeat touches, and by higher-timeframe
//     confluence. Only levels at or above the display threshold are drawn.
//
//  3) CLUSTERING AND TOUCH CONFIRMATION
//     New swings forming inside an existing level's merge distance are not drawn separately. They
//     merge into it, its touch count rises and its power rises with it. A price area the market
//     has respected five times is reported as stronger than one it touched once, which is how a
//     chart is actually read and something a single-swing model cannot express.
//
//  4) ZONES, NOT LINES
//     Real support and resistance is an area, not a decimal. Every level is drawn as a band whose
//     height scales with ATR, so the zone is proportionate to the instrument's own volatility on
//     the current timeframe. The centre line remains available for precision.
//
//  5) ROLE REVERSAL
//     When price closes decisively through a level, that level is not discarded. It flips: broken
//     resistance becomes support, broken support becomes resistance. Flipped levels are drawn in
//     their own colour and labelled with the flip, so the chart shows a level's full history
//     instead of forgetting it at the moment it often becomes most useful.
//
//  6) HIGHER-TIMEFRAME CONFLUENCE
//     Pivot levels from a higher timeframe of your choosing are requested and mapped onto the
//     current chart. When a local level sits within the confluence distance of one, it receives a
//     power bonus and is tagged. Levels agreed on by two timeframes are the levels that matter.
//
//  7) PSYCHOLOGICAL ROUND NUMBERS
//     Round price increments act as reference points in their own right. The engine selects a
//     sensible step automatically from the instrument's price magnitude and its ATR, or accepts a
//     manual step, and marks the round levels currently in range.
//
//  8) LIVE HOLD-RATE STATISTICS
//     The engine watches what actually happens each time price enters a level's zone. If price
//     leaves without closing through, that is a hold. If price closes decisively beyond, that is a
//     break. Results are accumulated per power tier and reported in the table, so you can see on
//     this chart, on this timeframe, how often a high-power level has actually held. This is an
//     observed record of what already happened, not a projection of what will.
//
//  9) PRESSURE METER
//     Where a bar closes inside its own range is a proxy for who controlled it, mapped to seven
//     states from Strong Sell through Balanced to Strong Buy. Because a single candle is a thin
//     sample, smoothing over several bars is available and enabled by default.
//
// 10) ALERTS
//     New level mapped, level broken, level flipped, price approaching a high-power level, and
//     pressure shifting into strong buying or strong selling.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   M A R K E T   A N D   T I M E F R A M E   C O M P A T I B I L I T Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  No pip value, point distance or instrument-specific constant appears anywhere in the logic.
//  Every distance is expressed in ATR multiples and every strength term is a ratio. The adaptive
//  window means detection sensitivity self-adjusts rather than needing retuning per timeframe.
//  The round-number step is derived from the instrument's own magnitude and volatility.
//
//  Many spot FX, CFD and metals feeds publish no traded volume. The participation component is
//  therefore supplied by a Universal Activity Engine which uses real volume where it exists, an
//  optional external reference symbol where you provide one, and otherwise a synthetic
//  participation estimate derived from range and candle efficiency. The active source is always
//  named on the summary table, so you always know exactly what you are reading.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L I V E   B E H A V I O U R   A N D   R E P A I N T I N G   S T A T E M E N T
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A swing can only be confirmed once the required bars have formed to its right. That is what a
//  swing is, and it is true of every pivot-based tool. Once confirmed, a level's price never
//  changes and its drawing never moves.
//
//  The elements that update live, tick by tick, are the ones that should: the pressure meter, the
//  proximity classification, the percentage distance on each label, the hold-rate statistics and
//  the summary table. Level power updates only when a new touch confirms the level, when
//  confluence is established, or when recency decay advances.
//
//  The higher-timeframe request uses lookahead off, so no future higher-timeframe data can reach
//  a past bar. Higher-timeframe levels appear only once their own bar has closed, which is the
//  correct and non-repainting behaviour.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D I S C L A I M E R
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  This tool is for educational and informational purposes only. It does not constitute financial
//  advice. Trading involves risk; past patterns do not guarantee future results. The hold-rate
//  statistics describe what has already happened on the loaded history and are not a prediction.
//  Use proper risk management and consult a licensed financial advisor before trading real
//  capital.
// ==============================================================================================

indicator("Adaptive Support Resistance", "ASR", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 300, max_lines_count = 300, max_labels_count = 300, max_bars_back = 500)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  I N P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gDet = "=====  ADAPTIVE DETECTION  ====="
minSwing = input.int(3,  "Minimum Swing Bars", minval = 2, maxval = 20, group = gDet, tooltip = "Used when volatility is high. Turns resolve fast, so fewer bars of confirmation are needed.")
maxSwing = input.int(10, "Maximum Swing Bars", minval = 3, maxval = 30, group = gDet, tooltip = "Used when volatility is low. Drift produces false turns, so more bars of confirmation are needed.")
volFast  = input.int(10, "Volatility Fast ATR", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = gDet)
volSlow  = input.int(50, "Volatility Slow ATR", minval = 5, maxval = 300, group = gDet)
atrLen   = input.int(14, "Scoring ATR Length",  minval = 2, maxval = 200, group = gDet)

gPow = "=====  LEVEL POWER MODEL  ====="
minPower   = input.float(4.0,  "Minimum Power To Display", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gPow, tooltip = "Levels below this are tracked internally but not drawn. Raise it to keep only the strongest structure.")
wImpulse   = input.float(0.45, "Weight - Displacement Impulse", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gPow)
wPartic    = input.float(0.30, "Weight - Participation",        minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gPow)
wReject    = input.float(0.25, "Weight - Rejection Quality",    minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gPow)
impNorm    = input.float(3.0,  "Impulse Saturation (x ATR)",       minval = 0.5, maxval = 15, step = 0.5, group = gPow)
partNorm   = input.float(2.5,  "Participation Saturation (x Avg)", minval = 1,   maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gPow)
recentBars = input.int(50,     "Full Weight Window (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 500, group = gPow)
decayFloor = input.float(0.50, "Recency Decay Floor", minval = 0.1, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gPow)
decaySpan  = input.int(200,    "Decay Span (bars)", minval = 20, maxval = 2000, group = gPow)
touchBonus = input.float(0.10, "Bonus Per Confirming Touch", minval = 0, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.01, group = gPow)
maxTouchB  = input.float(0.50, "Maximum Touch Bonus", minval = 0, maxval = 2, step = 0.05, group = gPow)
conflBonus = input.float(0.25, "Higher-Timeframe Confluence Bonus", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = gPow)

gLvl = "=====  LEVEL MANAGEMENT  ====="
mergeATR   = input.float(0.50, "Merge Distance (x ATR)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gLvl, tooltip = "New swings within this distance of an existing level merge into it as a confirming touch.")
maxPerSide = input.int(10, "Max Levels Per Side", minval = 1, maxval = 40, group = gLvl)
breakBuf   = input.float(0.25, "Break Buffer (x ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gLvl, tooltip = "How far beyond a level price must close before that level counts as resolved.")
flipOn     = input.bool(true, "Enable Role Reversal", group = gLvl, tooltip = "ON  : a broken resistance becomes support and a broken support becomes resistance, drawn in the flip colour.\nOFF : broken levels are retired from the chart.")
maxFlips   = input.int(2, "Max Flips Per Level", minval = 1, maxval = 6, group = gLvl, tooltip = "After this many role reversals the level is retired.")

gZone = "=====  ZONES  ====="
zoneOn    = input.bool(true, "Draw Levels As Zones", group = gZone)
zoneATR   = input.float(0.30, "Zone Half-Height (x ATR)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 2, step = 0.05, group = gZone, tooltip = "The zone scales with volatility, so it stays proportionate on every instrument and timeframe.")
zoneCentre= input.bool(true, "Show Zone Centre Line", group = gZone)
zoneExt   = input.int(20, "Zone Extension (bars)", minval = 0, maxval = 200, group = gZone)

gMtf = "=====  HIGHER-TIMEFRAME CONFLUENCE  ====="
mtfOn    = input.bool(true, "Enable Higher-Timeframe Levels", group = gMtf)
mtfTf    = input.timeframe("60", "Higher Timeframe", group = gMtf)
mtfLeft  = input.int(6, "HTF Pivot Left",  minval = 2, maxval = 30, group = gMtf, inline = "m")
mtfRight = input.int(6, "HTF Pivot Right", minval = 2, maxval = 30, group = gMtf, inline = "m")
mtfMax   = input.int(6, "Max HTF Levels Per Side", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gMtf)
conflATR = input.float(0.60, "Confluence Distance (x ATR)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 3, step = 0.05, group = gMtf)
mtfDraw  = input.bool(true, "Draw HTF Levels On Chart", group = gMtf)

gRnd = "=====  PSYCHOLOGICAL ROUND NUMBERS  ====="
roundOn   = input.bool(true, "Show Round Number Levels", group = gRnd)
roundAuto = input.bool(true, "Automatic Step", group = gRnd, tooltip = "Derives a sensible increment from the instrument's price magnitude and its ATR. Turn off to set the step manually.")
roundStepM= input.float(10.0, "Manual Step", minval = 0.00001, group = gRnd)
roundMult = input.float(8.0, "Auto Step Target (x ATR)", minval = 1, maxval = 60, step = 0.5, group = gRnd)
roundSpan = input.float(6.0, "Show Within (x ATR)", minval = 1, maxval = 40, step = 0.5, group = gRnd)

gStat = "=====  HOLD-RATE STATISTICS  ====="
statsOn   = input.bool(true, "Track Hold Rate By Power Tier", group = gStat, tooltip = "Records what actually happened each time price entered a level's zone on the loaded history. Observed record, not a projection.")
holdATR   = input.float(1.0, "Hold Confirmed At (x ATR)", minval = 0.2, maxval = 6, step = 0.1, group = gStat, tooltip = "How far price must travel back away from a zone before the test counts as held.")

gProx = "=====  PROXIMITY CLASSIFICATION  ====="
immATR = input.float(0.75, "Immediate Within (x ATR)",   minval = 0.1, maxval = 5,  step = 0.05, group = gProx)
stATR  = input.float(2.50, "Short-Term Within (x ATR)",  minval = 0.5, maxval = 15, step = 0.25, group = gProx)
mtATR  = input.float(6.00, "Medium-Term Within (x ATR)", minval = 1.0, maxval = 40, step = 0.5,  group = gProx)

gPres = "=====  PRESSURE METER  ====="
presSmooth = input.bool(true, "Smooth Pressure", group = gPres, tooltip = "ON averages the closing-position reading over several bars. A single candle is a thin sample, so smoothing is recommended.")
presLen    = input.int(5, "Smoothing Length", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = gPres)

gAlr = "=====  ALERTS  ====="
alertPower = input.float(7.0, "Approach Alert Minimum Power", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.5, group = gAlr)
approachATR= input.float(0.50, "Approach Distance (x ATR)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 5, step = 0.05, group = gAlr)

gAct = "=====  ACTIVITY SOURCE  ====="
actMode = input.string("Auto", "Participation Source", options = ["Auto", "Chart Volume Only", "External Symbol", "Synthetic Estimate"], group = gAct)
extSym  = input.symbol("", "External Volume Symbol", group = gAct)

gVis = "=====  VISUALS  ====="
showLabels = input.bool(true, "Show Level Labels", group = gVis)
showPct    = input.bool(true, "Show Percent Distance", group = gVis)
showPowTxt = input.bool(true, "Show Power Rating", group = gVis)
lblSize    = input.string("Tiny", "Label Size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group = gVis)
showTable  = input.bool(true, "Show Summary Table", group = gVis)
tablePos   = input.string("Top Right", "Table Position", options = ["Top Right", "Middle Right", "Bottom Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Left"], group = gVis)

gSty = "=====  STYLE  ====="
colRes   = input.color(#f6465d, "Resistance", group = gSty, inline = "a")
colSup   = input.color(#26e2a8, "Support",    group = gSty, inline = "a")
colFlipR = input.color(#ff9800, "Flipped To Resistance", group = gSty, inline = "b")
colFlipS = input.color(#00bcd4, "Flipped To Support",    group = gSty, inline = "b")
colMtf   = input.color(#b388ff, "HTF Level",     group = gSty, inline = "c")
colRound = input.color(#9e9e9e, "Round Number",  group = gSty, inline = "c")
colTxt   = input.color(color.white, "Label Text", group = gSty)
colTblBg = input.color(#0b1020, "Table Background", group = gSty, inline = "d")
colTblTx = input.color(#d1d4dc, "Table Text",       group = gSty, inline = "d")
colAcc   = input.color(#f0b90b, "Accent", group = gSty)

string szL = lblSize == "Small" ? size.small : lblSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : size.tiny

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  U N I V E R S A L   A C T I V I T Y   E N G I N E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float  rawVol  = nz(volume)
bool   hasReal = ta.cum(rawVol) > 0 and not na(volume)
string reqSym  = extSym == "" ? syminfo.tickerid : extSym
float  extRaw  = request.security(reqSym, timeframe.period, volume, ignore_invalid_symbol = true)
float  extVol  = nz(extRaw)
bool   hasExt  = extSym != "" and ta.cum(extVol) > 0

float trueR   = ta.tr(true)
float baseATR = ta.atr(20)
float bodyEff = trueR > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / trueR : 0.0
float synth   = baseATR > 0 ? math.max(0.0, (trueR / baseATR) * (0.55 + 0.45 * bodyEff) * 1000.0) : 0.0

string actName = "Synthetic"
float  actVol  = synth
if actMode == "Chart Volume Only"
    actVol  := rawVol
    actName := hasReal ? "Real" : "None"
else if actMode == "External Symbol"
    actVol  := extVol
    actName := hasExt ? "External" : "None"
else if actMode == "Synthetic Estimate"
    actVol  := synth
    actName := "Synthetic"
else
    if hasReal
        actVol  := rawVol
        actName := "Real"
    else if hasExt
        actVol  := extVol
        actName := "External"
    else
        actVol  := synth
        actName := "Synthetic"

float actAvg = ta.sma(actVol, 20)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A D A P T I V E   S W I N G   W I N D O W
//  High volatility -> fewer confirmation bars. Low volatility -> more confirmation bars.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float atrS     = ta.atr(atrLen)
float aFast    = ta.atr(volFast)
float aSlow    = ta.atr(volSlow)
float volRatio = aSlow > 0 ? aFast / aSlow : 1.0
float volRank  = nz(ta.percentrank(volRatio, 100), 50.0)
int   hiSw     = math.max(minSwing, maxSwing)
int   swingLen = math.max(minSwing, math.min(hiSw, int(math.round(hiSw - (hiSw - minSwing) * volRank / 100.0))))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P I V O T   Q U A L I F I C A T I O N   (manual, works on a dynamic window)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
isPivot(int len, bool isRes) =>
    float c  = isRes ? high[len] : low[len]
    bool  ok = not na(c)
    if ok
        for i = 1 to hiSw
            if i <= len
                float lft = isRes ? high[len + i] : low[len + i]
                float rgt = isRes ? high[len - i] : low[len - i]
                if na(lft) or na(rgt)
                    ok := false
                else if isRes
                    if lft > c or rgt >= c
                        ok := false
                else
                    if lft < c or rgt <= c
                        ok := false
    ok

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L E V E L   P O W E R   M O D E L
//  Dimensionless components only. No raw price term appears anywhere in this calculation, which
//  is why the score differentiates correctly on gold, indices, crypto and FX alike.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
basePower(int len, bool isRes) =>
    float a  = nz(atrS[len])
    float px = isRes ? high[len] : low[len]

    float extL = na
    float extR = na
    for i = 1 to hiSw
        if i <= len
            float vL = isRes ? low[len + i] : high[len + i]
            float vR = isRes ? low[len - i] : high[len - i]
            extL := na(extL) ? vL : (isRes ? math.min(extL, vL) : math.max(extL, vL))
            extR := na(extR) ? vR : (isRes ? math.min(extR, vR) : math.max(extR, vR))
    float approach = isRes ? px - nz(extL, px) : nz(extL, px) - px
    float depart   = isRes ? px - nz(extR, px) : nz(extR, px) - px
    float impulse  = a > 0 ? math.max(math.max(approach, depart), 0.0) / a : 0.0
    float compA    = math.min(impulse / math.max(impNorm, 0.1), 1.0)

    float av    = nz(actAvg[len])
    float ratio = av > 0 ? nz(actVol[len]) / av : 1.0
    float compB = math.min(ratio / math.max(partNorm, 0.1), 1.0)

    float rng  = nz(high[len]) - nz(low[len])
    float bodH = math.max(nz(open[len]), nz(close[len]))
    float bodL = math.min(nz(open[len]), nz(close[len]))
    float wick = isRes ? nz(high[len]) - bodH : bodL - nz(low[len])
    float compC = rng > 0 ? math.min(math.max(wick, 0.0) / rng * 2.0, 1.0) : 0.0

    float wSum  = math.max(wImpulse + wPartic + wReject, 0.0001)
    float blend = (compA * wImpulse + compB * wPartic + compC * wReject) / wSum
    math.max(0.0, math.min(10.0, blend * 10.0))

recency(int age) =>
    float r = 1.0
    if age > recentBars
        float over = age - recentBars
        r := math.max(decayFloor, 1.0 - (1.0 - decayFloor) * math.min(over / math.max(decaySpan, 1), 1.0))
    r

powerTier(float p) =>
    p >= 8.0 ? "Extreme" : p >= 6.0 ? "Very Strong" : p >= 4.0 ? "Strong" : p >= 2.0 ? "Moderate" : "Weak"

powerBar(float p) =>
    int n = math.max(1, math.min(5, int(math.round(p / 2.0))))
    string s = ""
    for i = 1 to 5
        s := s + (i <= n ? "|" : ".")
    s

proximity(float d, float a) =>
    float m = a > 0 ? d / a : 0.0
    m <= immATR ? "Immediate" : m <= stATR ? "Short-Term" : m <= mtATR ? "Medium-Term" : "Long-Term"

// statistics bucket: 0 = high power, 1 = medium, 2 = low
tierBucket(float p) =>
    p >= 7.0 ? 0 : p >= 4.0 ? 1 : 2

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  H I G H E R - T I M E F R A M E   L E V E L S
//  Requested with lookahead off. An HTF level appears only once its own bar has closed.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[htfPH, htfPL] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, mtfTf, [ta.pivothigh(mtfLeft, mtfRight), ta.pivotlow(mtfLeft, mtfRight)], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

var array<float> mtfRes = array.new<float>()
var array<float> mtfSup = array.new<float>()

if mtfOn and barstate.isconfirmed
    if not na(htfPH) and (mtfRes.size() == 0 or mtfRes.get(mtfRes.size() - 1) != htfPH)
        mtfRes.push(htfPH)
        while mtfRes.size() > mtfMax
            mtfRes.shift()
    if not na(htfPL) and (mtfSup.size() == 0 or mtfSup.get(mtfSup.size() - 1) != htfPL)
        mtfSup.push(htfPL)
        while mtfSup.size() > mtfMax
            mtfSup.shift()

nearHtf(float px, float tol) =>
    bool found = false
    if mtfRes.size() > 0
        for v in mtfRes
            if math.abs(v - px) <= tol
                found := true
    if mtfSup.size() > 0
        for v in mtfSup
            if math.abs(v - px) <= tol
                found := true
    found

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  L E V E L   R E G I S T R Y
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type Level
    float price
    bool  isRes
    int   born
    float raw
    int   touches
    int   flips
    bool  confl
    int   state
    int   testTier
    box   zn
    line  ln
    label lb

var array<Level> levels = array.new<Level>()

// observed hold and break counts by power tier
var array<int> statHold  = array.from(0, 0, 0)
var array<int> statBreak = array.from(0, 0, 0)

bool newRes  = false
bool newSup  = false
bool broke   = false
bool flipped = false

method scrub(Level v) =>
    box.delete(v.zn)
    line.delete(v.ln)
    label.delete(v.lb)

method livePower(Level v) =>
    float bonus = math.min(v.touches * touchBonus, maxTouchB) + (v.confl ? conflBonus : 0.0)
    math.min(10.0, v.raw * recency(bar_index - v.born) * (1.0 + bonus))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D E T E C T I O N ,   C L U S T E R I N G ,   T E S T   T R A C K I N G ,   R O L E   F L I P
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > hiSw * 2 + volSlow and not na(atrS) and atrS > 0
    float mergeD = atrS * mergeATR
    float zoneH  = atrS * zoneATR
    float brkD   = atrS * breakBuf

    // ---- new swings ----
    for pass = 0 to 1
        bool isRes = pass == 0
        if isPivot(swingLen, isRes)
            float px  = isRes ? high[swingLen] : low[swingLen]
            float raw = basePower(swingLen, isRes)
            int   bx  = bar_index - swingLen

            int hit = -1
            if levels.size() > 0
                for k = 0 to levels.size() - 1
                    Level v = levels.get(k)
                    if v.isRes == isRes and math.abs(v.price - px) <= mergeD
                        hit := k
            if hit >= 0
                Level v = levels.get(hit)
                v.touches += 1
                v.raw     := math.max(v.raw, raw)
                v.born    := bx
                v.price   := (v.price + px) / 2.0
                v.confl   := v.confl or (mtfOn and nearHtf(v.price, atrS * conflATR))
            else
                Level v = Level.new()
                v.price    := px
                v.isRes    := isRes
                v.born     := bx
                v.raw      := raw
                v.touches  := 1
                v.flips    := 0
                v.state    := 0
                v.testTier := 0
                v.confl    := mtfOn and nearHtf(px, atrS * conflATR)
                levels.push(v)
                if isRes
                    newRes := true
                else
                    newSup := true

    // ---- test tracking, break, role reversal ----
    if levels.size() > 0
        for k = levels.size() - 1 to 0
            Level v = levels.get(k)
            float zHi = v.price + zoneH
            float zLo = v.price - zoneH
            float p   = v.livePower()

            // price entering the zone starts a test
            if statsOn and v.state == 0 and high >= zLo and low <= zHi
                v.state    := 1
                v.testTier := tierBucket(p)

            bool gone = v.isRes ? close > v.price + brkD : close < v.price - brkD

            if gone
                broke := true
                if statsOn and v.state == 1
                    statBreak.set(v.testTier, statBreak.get(v.testTier) + 1)
                v.state := 0
                if flipOn and v.flips < maxFlips
                    v.isRes   := not v.isRes
                    v.flips   += 1
                    v.born    := bar_index
                    v.touches := math.max(1, v.touches)
                    flipped   := true
                else
                    v.scrub()
                    levels.remove(k)
            else if statsOn and v.state == 1
                // price has travelled back away from the zone without closing through it
                float away = v.isRes ? v.price - high : low - v.price
                if away >= atrS * holdATR
                    statHold.set(v.testTier, statHold.get(v.testTier) + 1)
                    v.state := 0

    // ---- per-side cap, newest kept ----
    int nR = 0
    int nS = 0
    if levels.size() > 0
        for k = levels.size() - 1 to 0
            Level v = levels.get(k)
            if v.isRes
                nR += 1
                if nR > maxPerSide
                    v.scrub()
                    levels.remove(k)
            else
                nS += 1
                if nS > maxPerSide
                    v.scrub()
                    levels.remove(k)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  P R E S S U R E   M E T E R
//  Where a bar closes inside its own range is a proxy for who controlled it. Smoothed by default,
//  because one candle is a very thin sample on which to judge control.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
float barRange = high - low
float closePos = barRange > 0 ? (close - low) / barRange : 0.5
float pressure = presSmooth ? nz(ta.sma(closePos, presLen), 0.5) : closePos

string presTxt = pressure >= 0.85 ? "Strong Buy" : pressure >= 0.68 ? "Buying Dominance" : pressure >= 0.56 ? "Weak Buying" : pressure > 0.44 ? "Balanced" : pressure > 0.32 ? "Weak Selling" : pressure > 0.15 ? "Selling Dominance" : "Strong Sell"
color  presCol = pressure >= 0.56 ? colSup : pressure > 0.44 ? colTblTx : colRes

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  R O U N D   N U M B E R   E N G I N E
//  The step is derived from the instrument's own magnitude and volatility, so it is sensible on
//  gold, on an index, on a currency pair and on a sub-dollar altcoin without configuration.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
niceStep(float target) =>
    float t = math.max(target, 1e-10)
    float e = math.pow(10, math.floor(math.log(t) / math.log(10)))
    float m = t / e
    float n = m < 1.5 ? 1.0 : m < 3.5 ? 2.0 : m < 7.5 ? 5.0 : 10.0
    n * e

float roundStep = roundAuto ? niceStep(nz(atrS, 1.0) * roundMult) : roundStepM

var array<line>  rndLn = array.new<line>()
var array<label> rndLb = array.new<label>()

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D R A W I N G   A N D   L I V E   U P D A T E S
//  Level prices are fixed at detection. What refreshes here is proximity, percent distance, the
//  decayed power reading and the zone geometry, all functions of current price and current bar.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var float sumR = 0.0
var float sumS = 0.0
var float maxR = 0.0
var float maxS = 0.0
var int   cntR = 0
var int   cntS = 0
var int   cntF = 0
var int   cntC = 0
var float latR = na
var float latS = na
var float latRP = 0.0
var float latSP = 0.0
bool approachAlert = false

if barstate.islast
    sumR := 0.0
    sumS := 0.0
    maxR := 0.0
    maxS := 0.0
    cntR := 0
    cntS := 0
    cntF := 0
    cntC := 0
    latR := na
    latS := na
    latRP := 0.0
    latSP := 0.0

    float zoneH = nz(atrS, 0.0) * zoneATR
    int   newestR = -1
    int   newestS = -1

    // ---- mapped levels ----
    if levels.size() > 0
        for k = 0 to levels.size() - 1
            Level v = levels.get(k)
            float p = v.livePower()
            float d = math.abs(close - v.price)
            bool  isFlip = v.flips > 0
            color c = isFlip ? (v.isRes ? colFlipR : colFlipS) : (v.isRes ? colRes : colSup)

            if v.isRes
                cntR += 1
                sumR += p
                maxR := math.max(maxR, p)
                if newestR < 0 or v.born > levels.get(newestR).born
                    newestR := k
            else
                cntS += 1
                sumS += p
                maxS := math.max(maxS, p)
                if newestS < 0 or v.born > levels.get(newestS).born
                    newestS := k
            if isFlip
                cntF += 1
            if v.confl
                cntC += 1

            if p >= alertPower and d <= nz(atrS, 0.0) * approachATR
                approachAlert := true

            v.scrub()

            if p >= minPower
                if zoneOn
                    v.zn := box.new(v.born, v.price + zoneH, bar_index + zoneExt, v.price - zoneH, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(c, 55), border_width = 1, bgcolor = color.new(c, 86))
                if zoneCentre or not zoneOn
                    v.ln := line.new(v.born, v.price, bar_index + zoneExt, v.price, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(c, 25), width = 1, style = zoneOn ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid)
                if showLabels
                    string head = isFlip ? (v.isRes ? "FLIPPED RESISTANCE" : "FLIPPED SUPPORT") : (v.isRes ? "RESISTANCE" : "SUPPORT")
                    string txt = head + "\n" + str.tostring(v.price, format.mintick) + "\n" + proximity(d, nz(atrS, 0.0))
                    if showPct
                        float pct = close != 0 ? (v.price - close) / close * 100.0 : 0.0
                        txt := txt + "\n" + (pct >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(pct, "#.##") + "%"
                    if showPowTxt
                        txt := txt + "\n" + powerBar(p) + "  " + powerTier(p) + " " + str.tostring(p, "#.#")
                    string tags = ""
                    if v.touches > 1
                        tags := tags + "  x" + str.tostring(v.touches)
                    if v.confl
                        tags := tags + "  HTF"
                    if isFlip
                        tags := tags + "  flip" + str.tostring(v.flips)
                    if tags != ""
                        txt := txt + "\n" + tags
                    v.lb := label.new(v.born, v.isRes ? v.price + zoneH : v.price - zoneH, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = v.isRes ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = color.new(c, 12), textcolor = colTxt, size = szL)

    if newestR >= 0
        latR  := levels.get(newestR).price
        latRP := levels.get(newestR).livePower()
    if newestS >= 0
        latS  := levels.get(newestS).price
        latSP := levels.get(newestS).livePower()

    // ---- higher-timeframe levels ----
    if rndLn.size() > 0
        for l in rndLn
            line.delete(l)
        rndLn.clear()
    if rndLb.size() > 0
        for l in rndLb
            label.delete(l)
        rndLb.clear()

    if mtfOn and mtfDraw
        if mtfRes.size() > 0
            for v in mtfRes
                rndLn.push(line.new(bar_index - 60, v, bar_index + zoneExt, v, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colMtf, 35), width = 2, style = line.style_dashed))
                rndLb.push(label.new(bar_index + zoneExt, v, "HTF R " + str.tostring(v, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colMtf, 20), textcolor = colTxt, size = size.tiny))
        if mtfSup.size() > 0
            for v in mtfSup
                rndLn.push(line.new(bar_index - 60, v, bar_index + zoneExt, v, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colMtf, 35), width = 2, style = line.style_dashed))
                rndLb.push(label.new(bar_index + zoneExt, v, "HTF S " + str.tostring(v, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colMtf, 20), textcolor = colTxt, size = size.tiny))

    // ---- psychological round numbers in range ----
    if roundOn and roundStep > 0 and not na(atrS)
        float span = atrS * roundSpan
        float first = math.floor((close - span) / roundStep) * roundStep
        for i = 0 to 40
            float lvl = first + roundStep * i
            if lvl > close + span
                break
            if lvl >= close - span and lvl > 0
                rndLn.push(line.new(bar_index - 60, lvl, bar_index + zoneExt, lvl, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(colRound, 55), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted))
                rndLb.push(label.new(bar_index + zoneExt, lvl, "R# " + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(colRound, 35), textcolor = colTxt, size = size.tiny))

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  S U M M A R Y   T A B L E
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var table tbl = na

tablePosition() =>
    tablePos == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : tablePos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : tablePos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : tablePos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : position.top_right

holdRate(int bucket) =>
    int h = statHold.get(bucket)
    int b = statBreak.get(bucket)
    int t = h + b
    t > 0 ? str.tostring(h * 100.0 / t, "#") + "% (" + str.tostring(t) + ")" : "-"

if barstate.islast and showTable
    table.delete(tbl)
    int rows = statsOn ? 11 : 8
    tbl := table.new(tablePosition(), 2, rows, border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(colTblTx, 82), frame_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(colTblTx, 72))

    color bgH = color.new(colTblBg, 0)
    color bgR = color.new(colTblBg, 12)

    float avgR = cntR > 0 ? sumR / cntR : na
    float avgS = cntS > 0 ? sumS / cntS : na

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 0, "ADAPTIVE SUPPORT RESISTANCE", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colAcc, text_size = size.small)
    table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 0, 1, 0)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 1, "RESISTANCE", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colRes, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 1, "Total: " + str.tostring(cntR) + "   Max: " + (cntR > 0 ? str.tostring(maxR, "#.#") : "-"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 2, "SUPPORT", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colSup, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 2, "Total: " + str.tostring(cntS) + "   Max: " + (cntS > 0 ? str.tostring(maxS, "#.#") : "-"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 3, "Avg Power", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 3, "R: " + (na(avgR) ? "-" : str.tostring(avgR, "#.#")) + "   S: " + (na(avgS) ? "-" : str.tostring(avgS, "#.#")), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 4, "Latest R", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 4, na(latR) ? "-" : str.tostring(latR, format.mintick) + "   " + str.tostring(latRP, "#.#"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colRes, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 5, "Latest S", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 5, na(latS) ? "-" : str.tostring(latS, format.mintick) + "   " + str.tostring(latSP, "#.#"), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colSup, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 6, "Flipped / HTF", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 6, str.tostring(cntF) + " flipped   " + str.tostring(cntC) + " confluent", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = cntC > 0 ? colMtf : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

    table.cell(tbl, 0, 7, "Pressure", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(tbl, 1, 7, presTxt + "   " + str.tostring(pressure * 100, "#") + "%", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = presCol, text_size = size.tiny)

    if statsOn
        table.cell(tbl, 0, 8, "OBSERVED HOLD RATE", bgcolor = bgH, text_color = colAcc, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.merge_cells(tbl, 0, 8, 1, 8)

        table.cell(tbl, 0, 9, "Power 7-10  |  4-7", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(tbl, 1, 9, holdRate(0) + "   |   " + holdRate(1), bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

        table.cell(tbl, 0, 10, "Power 0-4  |  Window/Src", bgcolor = bgR, text_color = colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)
        table.cell(tbl, 1, 10, holdRate(2) + "   |   " + str.tostring(swingLen) + "b " + actName, bgcolor = bgR, text_color = actName == "Synthetic" ? colAcc : colTblTx, text_size = size.tiny)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A L E R T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
alertcondition(newRes,  "ASR - New Resistance", "Adaptive Support Resistance: a new resistance level was mapped on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(newSup,  "ASR - New Support",    "Adaptive Support Resistance: a new support level was mapped on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(broke,   "ASR - Level Broken",   "Adaptive Support Resistance: price resolved through a mapped level on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(flipped, "ASR - Level Flipped",  "Adaptive Support Resistance: a level changed role after being broken on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(approachAlert, "ASR - Approaching High-Power Level", "Adaptive Support Resistance: price is approaching a high-power level on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(pressure >= 0.85 and pressure[1] < 0.85, "ASR - Strong Buying Pressure",  "Adaptive Support Resistance: pressure moved into strong buying on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")
alertcondition(pressure <= 0.15 and pressure[1] > 0.15, "ASR - Strong Selling Pressure", "Adaptive Support Resistance: pressure moved into strong selling on {{ticker}} {{interval}}.")

if newRes
    alert("ASR New Resistance - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if newSup
    alert("ASR New Support - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if broke
    alert("ASR Level Broken - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if flipped
    alert("ASR Level Flipped - " + syminfo.ticker + " " + timeframe.period, alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  D A T A   W I N D O W   O U T P U T S
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
plot(swingLen,      "Adaptive Swing Window", color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(pressure,      "Pressure (0-1)",        color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(levels.size(), "Levels Tracked",        color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(roundStep,     "Round Number Step",     color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(atrS,          "Scoring ATR",           color = color.new(color.orange, 100), display = display.data_window)